Third-party components
======================

This project builds on code from several sources. This file records what
came from where, under what terms, and what was changed.

InfoNES
-------

  Core/InfoNES/

NES emulator by TMK, originally released in 2000 as freeware. The copy
here comes from the PSP port (https://github.com/PSP-Archive/InfoNES),
which is the most widely circulated variant of the source.

InfoNES has no formal open-source licence. It has been distributed
publicly as freeware for over two decades and ported to many platforms
(see the list in https://github.com/jay-kumogata/InfoNES). If you intend
to use it commercially, establish the licensing position yourself.

Changes made for this port:

  - InfoNES.c
      * InfoNES_DrawLine() skips scanlines past NES_DISP_HEIGHT, which
        is smaller than a full frame (see the memory notes in the
        README). Without this the PPU writes past the end of the frame
        buffer.
      * InfoNES_Main() restored to a plain loop. The PSP port had the
        loop commented out and called InfoNES_Init() inside it, which
        reset the CPU on every iteration.
      * The FrameCnt == 0 guard on DrawLine() and LoadFrame() was
        removed — it stopped rendering after the first frame.
      * APU_Reg indices masked to 0x1f. The PSP port indexed APU_Reg
        with full 16-bit addresses, overflowing a 24-byte array.
      * RAM, SRAM, PPURAM and ChrBuf placed in CCM, to keep SRAM1 free
        for the DMA-visible frame buffer.

  - InfoNES_pAPU.h
      * APU_EVENT_MAX reduced from 15000 to 32. The event queue was
        120 KB — larger than the entire chip.

  - K6502_rw.h
      * OAM DMA now costs 514 cycles, matching hardware. Without it,
        games that rely on sprite DMA timing misbehave.

  - InfoNES_Mapper.c
      * Only mapper 0 is compiled in; the rest are #if 0-ed out. Several
        mappers declare large static buffers that overflow RAM here.
        The mapper source files are all still present.

  - InfoNES_pAPU.c
      * Audio is stubbed out at the HAL layer (nes_port.c), so the APU
        is never driven. The core is otherwise untouched.

FatFs
-----

  Drivers/FatFs/

Generic FAT filesystem module by ChaN (http://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/),
BSD-style licence. Used only by the (currently unused) SD card driver.

Configuration changed in ffconf.h:

  - FF_CODE_PAGE 437 (US OEM)
  - FF_USE_LFN 0 and FF_USE_FIND 0, to avoid the Unicode conversion
    tables

STMicroelectronics HAL and CMSIS
--------------------------------

  Not vendored — the build pulls these from the STM32CubeF4 firmware
  package (STM32Cube_FW_F4_V1.28.3 by default). BSD-3-Clause.

  Core/system_stm32f4xx.c is copied from that package into this tree so
  the include order works without CubeMX.

  stm32f4xx_hal_conf.h and STM32F407VETX_FLASH.ld are new files written
  for this project; the linker script defines the unusual SRAM1/CCM
  split described in the README.
